# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for tsan.sh. Each entry names one function and
# says why its report is not a bug in the output; anything else fails the gate.
#
# AVM's AVX2 MHCCP neighbour fetch (av2/common/x86/cfl_avx2.c) reads the
# reconstructed luma above and left of a block 32 columns at a time, past the
# region it was asked for (ref_width); at a tile's right edge that reaches
# into the next tile, which another thread is coding. The values read past
# ref_width are never used (the MHCCP derivation reads ref_width / 2 columns),
# and multi-threaded encodes of these paths give the one-thread stream
# (avm-bench results/determinism-rd.*). An upstream kernel; MHCCP runs at
# realtime speeds up to 8 and in good quality, not at 9 and 10.
race:av2_mhccp_implicit_fetch_neighbor_luma_420_avx2
